                    The HTML <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> element identifies form
                    controls and improves usability and accessibility. The most
                    common approach is to connect a label's <code>for</code>
                    attribute with the control's <code>id</code>. Labels can be
                    associated with text inputs, email fields, passwords,
                    textareas, dropdowns, radio buttons, checkboxes, dates, files,
                    and other form controls. Proper label associations make forms
